		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4781&amp;p=35888#p35888"><![CDATA[
Hi everyone,<br><br>I've just tested the APRS transmission from my RT-3S w/ OpenGD77 to my Anytone878.<br>You need to switch the OpenGD77 APRS compression "Off" to enable the correct GPS coordinates on the Anytone.<br>With APRS compression "On" the Anytone shows a nonsense GPS location.<br><br>I've also checked my RT-3S APRS function with a local Digipeater. It successfully decodes the GPS coordinates independent of compression "On" or "Off".<br><br>Best regards<br>Fritz<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8162">DK9RC</a> — Sun Feb 23, 2025 10:38 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
