Hi Daniel,<br><br>Thank you for your reply and for pointing out the mismatch in the images I provided—I apologize for the confusion.<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2821&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-21 120323.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2822&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-21 120600.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2823&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="image0.jpeg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>and here the log from direwolf :<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>IU0TWZ-7 audio level = 27(5/3)    ___||||||[0.5] IU0TWZ-7&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1:!\9C+uQYd@&amp;  !Fabio RT3S FIXEDPosition, I=Igte IGate R=RX T=1hopTX 2=2hopTXN 41 46.8000, E 012 22.8000Fabio RT3S FIXED&gt;&gt;&gt; Monitored Unproto Information to AGWPE client application 0, total length = 140        portx = 0, datakind = 'U', pid = 0x00        call_from = "IU0TWZ-7", call_to = "APOG77"        data_len = 104, user_reserved = 0, data =  000:  20 31 3a 46 6d 20 49 55 30 54 57 5a 2d 37 20 54   1:Fm IU0TWZ-7 T  010:  6f 20 41 50 4f 47 37 37 20 56 69 61 20 57 49 44  o APOG77 Via WID  020:  45 31 2d 31 20 3c 55 49 20 70 69 64 3d 46 30 20  E1-1 &lt;UI pid=F0  030:  4c 65 6e 3d 33 30 20 50 46 3d 30 20 3e 5b 31 32  Len=30 PF=0 &gt;[12  040:  3a 31 35 3a 35 31 5d 0d 21 5c 39 43 2b 75 51 59  :15:51].!\9C+uQY  050:  64 40 26 20 20 21 46 61 62 69 6f 20 52 54 33 53  d@&amp;  !Fabio RT3S  060:  20 46 49 58 45 44 0d 00                           FIXED..ax25_delete, seq=30, called from /home/John/src/direwolf-dev/src/dlq.c 1195, new_count=33, delete_count=33dlq_remove (type=7, chan=0, ...)</code></pre></div>I’ve double-checked the setup, and I can confirm that the Retevis RT3S GPS is transmitting correctly because when I use Direwolf as the decoder, it processes the APRS packet without issues. However, the problem arises when decoding the message with my Anytone 878 II. The packet appears corrupted or misinterpreted on the Anytone, as shown in the new screenshot attached.<br><br>Please note that I am testing in direct mode on the Anytone since the nearest APRS beacon is too far, and I cannot reach it.<br><br>This suggests the issue might not be with the RT3S but rather with the way the Anytone is decoding the APRS packet.<br><br>I would appreciate any insights or advice on how to resolve this discrepancy.<br><br>Thanks again for your help!<br><br>Fabio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7833">IU0TWZ</a> — Tue Jan 21, 2025 11:14 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
