Dear all,<br>My name is Fabio, and I am writing from Rome, Italy. I am fascinated by this amazing software and have been exploring its various features.<br>I am currently using a Retevis RT-3S GPS with the latest firmware version (25-01-19). I have configured the parameters for APRS and set a fixed location, as shown in the attached image. <div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2818&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-20 235941.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>I have also set up the channel configuration according to the settings in the second image.<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2820&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-21 000058.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>However, when I send an APRS message, the encoding seems incorrect. This is evident in the Soundmodem (KISS emulator), and for confirmation, I also tested it with my Anytone 878 II, which can decode APRS. Both show that the coordinates and message are interpreted incorrectly<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2819&amp;sid=3ee69a017a430eb912dcf73b31ac3e10" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-21 000029.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><br>Could anyone assist me in resolving this issue?<br><br>Thank you in advance for your help!<br>Fabio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7833">IU0TWZ</a> — Tue Jan 21, 2025 12:49 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
